# MLS Bolivia — MVP Business Specification

> This document defines what the product does and how each part works at a business level.
> It contains no technical or design decisions. It is the single source of truth for development.

---

## 1. What the product is

A multi-tenant SaaS platform for Bolivian real estate developers (constructoras) that combines two things:

1. **Internal Commercial CRM** — to manage clients who come directly to the developer (through the sales office, social media, referrals, etc.)
2. **Broker Marketplace** — to allow independent external real estate brokers to access the developer's inventory, generate commercial proposals, and declare reservation interest on specific units.

Both sides share the same real-time inventory. A unit reserved by a broker disappears from the internal CRM and vice versa. There are no separate inventories.

The product is sold to developers as a management tool. Brokers access it for free or with a paid plan, but the primary paying customer is the developer.

---

## 2. System actors

The system has four types of users with distinct responsibilities.

### Super Admin

The platform administrator — the team that operates the SaaS. There is only one at the platform level and they do not belong to any developer company.

Can do:

- Create and manage developer accounts
- Activate or deactivate developer accounts
- Approve or reject broker registration requests
- Suspend brokers with abusive behavior
- View global metrics across the entire platform

Cannot see private client information from any developer.

---

### Developer Admin

The commercial manager or sales director of a developer company. There can be more than one per developer.

Can do:

- Create, edit, and publish projects
- Load and manage units for each project
- View all direct leads of their developer
- Assign leads to internal sales executives
- View and manage all broker reservation intents
- Approve or reject reservation intents
- Manage which brokers have access to private projects
- Mark commissions as paid
- View the post-sale history of their projects

---

### Developer Sales (Internal Sales Executive)

The developer's internal salesperson. Works under the Developer Admin.

Can do:

- View the project and unit inventory of their developer
- Register new leads and manage the ones assigned to them
- Advance the status of their leads through the pipeline
- Generate commercial proposals for their clients
- Record payments received from their assigned clients
- View the post-sale status of units they sold

Cannot:

- Approve or reject broker intents
- Change unit prices
- View leads assigned to other executives — they only see their own and unassigned ones

---

### Broker (External Agent)

An independent real estate agent who looks for projects to sell to their own clients. Not an employee of any developer.

Can do:

- View the public project catalog from all developers
- View the detail of each project and its available units
- Generate commercial proposals for their clients
- Declare a reservation intent on a unit (PRO plan only)
- View the status of their own intents
- Join the waitlist for a unit that already has an active intent
- View the status of their commissions

Cannot:

- View the direct leads of any developer
- View internal notes on any unit
- View other brokers' intents
- Change any project or unit data

**Broker plans:**

- **FREE**: can view projects and generate commercial proposals. Cannot declare reservation intents.
- **PRO**: everything in FREE plus declare reservation intents and join waitlists.

**Account approval:** Brokers self-register on the platform but their account remains pending until the Super Admin manually approves it. An unapproved broker can do nothing beyond seeing a pending-approval screen.

**Reputation:** Every broker has a visible counter of intent cancellations in the last 30 days. This number is visible to the Developer Admin when reviewing an intent. It does not trigger automatic blocks — it is purely informational for the developer to factor into their decision.

---

## 3. Module: Projects and Inventory

This module is the foundation of everything. Without it, nothing else works.

### Projects

A developer can have multiple active projects at the same time. A project represents a complete building or real estate development (for example, "Edificio Vitrubio").

Each project has:

- Name, description, address, neighborhood, and city
- Project status
- Visibility (public or private)
- Estimated delivery date
- Total number of floors
- List of building-level amenities (pool, gym, rooftop, BBQ area, coworking, lobby, 24h security, visitor parking, pet-friendly, smart home)
- Project images and downloadable brochure
- Base commission percentage for external brokers
- Deadline in business hours that a broker has to advance after declaring an intent

**Project statuses:**

- **DRAFT**: the developer is still configuring it. Not visible to anyone external.
- **PUBLISHED**: visible according to its visibility setting (public or private). Brokers and executives can see its units and generate proposals.
- **PAUSED**: the project stops accepting new intents. Existing active intents are suspended — not cancelled — the countdown freezes. Units do not change status.
- **CLOSED**: terminal status. No actions can be taken on the project. Active intents are automatically cancelled and units become unavailable.

**Project visibility:**

- **Public**: any registered and approved broker can see it and work with it.
- **Private**: only brokers explicitly invited by the developer can see it. Others are unaware of its existence.

---

### Units

A unit is any individual asset that can be sold within a project: apartments, offices, commercial spaces, parking spots, and storage rooms.

Each unit has:

- A human-readable identifier (e.g., "Apt 301", "E-04", "Shop 02")
- Unit type
- Current status
- Price in US dollars
- Own commission percentage (if different from the project base percentage)
- Physical attributes specific to its type
- Unit-specific images
- Internal notes (visible only to the developer — never to brokers)

**Unit types:**

- Apartment
- Office
- Commercial space
- Parking spot
- Storage room

**Unit statuses:**

- **AVAILABLE**: no one has active interest. Can be quoted and reserved.
- **WITH INTEREST**: there is exactly one active reservation intent on it. Only one, never two simultaneously.
- **RESERVED**: an intent was approved. The unit is committed to a buyer.
- **SOLD**: terminal status. The sale is fully closed.
- **SUSPENDED**: temporarily withdrawn from the market by the developer's decision. Does not accept new intents.
- **UNAVAILABLE**: terminal status. The unit is not for sale (own use, donation, etc.).

**Critical rule:** At no point can there be two active intents on the same unit. The system must guarantee this without exception.

**Price changes:** Every time a unit's price changes, the system records the previous price, the new price, who changed it, and why. This history is immutable and serves as evidence in case of disputes. If there is an active intent at the time of the price change, the broker receives a notification with the exact amount of the change. The intent is not automatically cancelled — the broker decides whether to continue or cancel.

