## 4. Module: Commercial CRM (Direct Leads)

This module manages clients who come to the developer through their own channels, without the involvement of an external broker.

### Registering a lead

When a client shows direct interest, the internal executive registers them as a lead with:

- Full name
- National ID (CI) — this is the key field for detecting duplicates with broker clients
- Phone number
- Email (optional)
- How they arrived: walk-in at sales office, phone call, social media, referral, website, other
- Units they are interested in
- Initial notes

The lead is assigned to an executive. The Developer Admin can reassign it to another executive at any time.

### Lead pipeline

A lead advances through these statuses in order:

1. **NEW** — just registered, no contact yet
2. **CONTACTED** — the executive has already communicated with them
3. **VISITED** — the client visited the project or sales office physically
4. **QUOTED** — a formal commercial proposal was generated for them
5. **RESERVED** — they made the reservation payment
6. **LOST** — no longer interested or chose another option

A lead can move to LOST from any status. A lead in RESERVED status cannot go backwards.

Every status change is recorded with date, time, and who made the change.

### Commercial proposal for a direct lead

The executive can generate a commercial proposal for their lead in the same way a broker does. The document includes the client's data, the selected unit, the price at the time of generation, and the generation date. This document can be shared directly via WhatsApp.

The generation date and time is the official record that this client was attended by this executive for this unit.

### Duplicate detection

When a new lead is registered, the system compares their national ID against:

- All existing leads for that developer
- All clients mentioned in active or recent broker intents (last 90 days) for that developer

If a match is found, the system shows a visible alert to the executive registering the lead and to the Developer Admin. The alert indicates who first registered the client and through which channel (internal executive or broker). The developer decides what to do — the system does not resolve the conflict automatically.

---

## 5. Module: Broker Marketplace

This module manages the relationship between external brokers and developer projects.

### Commercial proposal (FREE and PRO plan)

Any broker with an approved account can generate a commercial proposal for any available unit in any public project. The proposal does not lock the unit.

The proposal includes:

- The broker's client data (name, national ID, phone)
- The selected unit or set of units
- The price at the time of generation — frozen at that moment. If the price changes later, the document reflects the price on the day it was generated.
- Estimated commission for the broker
- Generation date and time
- Valid for 30 days

The document can be shared directly via WhatsApp.

The generation date and time is the official record that this broker presented this unit to this client. It serves as evidence in commission disputes.

### Reservation intent (PRO plan only)

When a broker has a serious client who wants to commit to a specific unit, they declare a reservation intent.

When declaring the intent, the broker provides:

- Which unit or units they want to reserve
- Client data: full name, national ID, phone, optional email
- Whether the client already has secured financing
- Whether the client has already visited the project physically

At the moment the intent is declared:

- The unit changes from AVAILABLE to WITH INTEREST
- All other brokers who were viewing that unit receive a notification: "This unit just received a reservation intent"
- The Developer Admin receives a notification with the broker's and client's data
- A countdown timer begins

### Intent on multiple units (bundle)

A broker can declare an intent on several units at the same time (for example: Apartment 301 + Parking E-04 + Storage D-02). This is called a bundle.

A bundle is atomic: it is approved or rejected as a whole. It is not possible to approve only the apartment and reject the parking spot. If the intent is cancelled or expires, all units in the bundle are released at the same time.

For a bundle to be valid, all units must be in AVAILABLE status at the exact same instant. If any of them already has another active intent, the entire operation cannot proceed.

### Intent countdown timer

The developer defines per project how many business hours they have to respond to an intent. The minimum is 24 business hours and the maximum is 168 business hours (equivalent to one full work week).

Business hours are counted only on weekdays (Monday through Friday), excluding Bolivian national holidays.

The countdown starts at the exact moment the intent is declared.

The Developer Admin receives two reminders before it expires:

- First when 50% of the time has elapsed
- Second when 75% of the time has elapsed

If the Developer Admin does not respond before the deadline, the intent expires automatically. Units return to AVAILABLE. Both the broker and the Developer Admin receive a notification stating the intent expired due to no response.

**Timer pause:** If the project moves to PAUSED status, the countdown for all active intents freezes. When the project returns to PUBLISHED, the countdown resumes from where it left off. The intent is not cancelled — only paused.

### Approval and rejection

The Developer Admin reviews the intent and decides.

**If approved:**

- The unit moves to RESERVED status
- The intent status becomes APPROVED
- A commission record is automatically created for the corresponding amount
- Brokers on the waitlist for that unit receive a notification: "This unit has been reserved"

**If rejected:**

- A mandatory reason must be selected: client not qualified, incomplete data, broker not enabled, taken internally, other
- An optional free-text note can be added
- The unit returns to AVAILABLE
- If there is a waitlist, the next broker in line is notified
- The broker receives a notification with the rejection reason

### Cancellation by the broker

The broker can cancel their own intent at any time before it is approved or rejected. Upon cancellation, the unit returns to AVAILABLE and the broker's cancellation counter for the last 30 days increases by one.

### Waitlist

If a unit already has an active intent (WITH INTEREST status), a PRO broker can join the waitlist for that unit.

The waitlist is strictly first-come, first-served based on registration time. The position does not change once assigned.

When the unit becomes free (due to cancellation, rejection, or expiration of the previous intent), the first broker on the list receives a notification. They have 2 hours to declare their own intent. If they do not act within that window, their spot is discarded and the next broker in line is notified. This continues until someone acts or the list is exhausted.

When a unit moves to RESERVED or SOLD, all brokers on the waitlist receive a notification: "This unit is no longer available" and their waitlist entries are discarded.

### Access to private projects

For projects with PRIVATE visibility, the developer manually manages which brokers have access.

The Developer Admin can invite a broker by name or email. The broker receives a notification and can accept or ignore the invitation.

The Developer Admin can revoke a broker's access at any time, with one exception: they cannot revoke it if that broker has an ACTIVE or APPROVED intent within that project. The system blocks the action and shows which intent is blocking it.

